{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1 and U2: Introduce configuration properties classes for CodeGen Options and Merge Options, using Spring's @ConfigurationProperties for binding.",
    "For U3: Add a timeout parameter to job configuration and implement enforcement using Spring's TaskExecutor with a timeout mechanism or a custom thread monitor.",
    "For U4: Create a new Processor/Job component that executes SQL statements/scripts via Spring's JdbcTemplate or ScriptUtils, supporting both inline statements and external script files.",
    "For U5: Extend the existing JDBC item reader (e.g., NameColumnJdbcItemReader) to allow injection of a custom RowMapper<Tuple> and modify afterPropertySet to use the provided mapper. Provide a default RowMapper implementation that adds timestamp and delete flag fields.",
    "For U6: Integrate Spring Expression Language (SpEL) for dynamic directory/file naming, using a common expression resolver that can access job parameters, system properties, and runtime data.",
    "For U7: Modify the CSV writer to support a configurable escape character (e.g., backslash) and ensure proper escaping of delimiters, quotes, and newlines for Hive/HAWQ compatibility.",
    "For U8: Refactor MessageBus transformation logic to minimize object allocation, use streaming transformations where possible, and optimize serialization/deserialization. Consider introducing a MessageTransformer interface with efficient implementations."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The project is an existing Spring-based batch processing application (likely using Spring Batch) with a codebase that already includes CodeGen, Merge, Job execution, JDBC readers, MessageBus, and CSV writing components.",
    "The development team (single developer) is familiar with the codebase, Spring Framework, Spring Batch, and related technologies.",
    "Development environment, build system (Maven/Gradle), and CI/CD pipeline are already set up and require no changes for this increment.",
    "Each user story will require design, implementation, unit testing, integration testing, and documentation updates.",
    "Some features share common infrastructure (e.g., expression evaluation for U6 may be reused elsewhere).",
    "No major architectural changes are required beyond the refactoring in U8.",
    "Effort estimates are for a single developer performing all work personally.",
    "Third-party libraries (e.g., for CSV parsing) are already included and can be extended."
  ],
